<h2>Proximity is the whole advantage</h2>
<p>Bangladesh is India's closest major export market, and almost everything about the trade follows from that. Sea transit to Chattogram runs 2–5 days. Land routes through Petrapole–Benapole can move goods in 1–3 days from West Bengal. Freight is a small fraction of landed cost compared with any other market we serve.</p>

<p>That structural advantage is why Bangladesh consistently ranks among the top destinations for Indian onion, lentils, cumin, turmeric and pulses — and why Bangladeshi buyers feel Indian supply disruptions faster and harder than anyone else.</p>

<h2>Sea or land — a real decision, not a formality</h2>
<p>Most exporters default to one or the other out of habit. It's worth thinking about:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Sea to Chattogram</strong> suits full-container volumes, goods sourced in western or southern India, and buyers with established port clearance arrangements.</li>
  <li><strong>Land ports</strong> (Petrapole–Benapole, Hili, Burimari) are faster and often cheaper for goods sourced in eastern India, but throughput varies with congestion and documentation practice differs from sea freight.</li>
</ul>
<p>Tell us where the goods are being sourced and what volume you need, and we'll recommend a routing rather than defaulting.</p>

<h2>Export-policy exposure cuts both ways</h2>
<p>Because Bangladesh depends heavily on Indian supply for several staples — onion above all — it's the market most directly affected when India restricts exports. India has imposed minimum export prices, duties and outright bans on onion at various points.</p>
<p>We won't quote Bangladesh onion business as though those conditions were settled. We confirm the position at order time, and we'd encourage any buyer building a recurring programme on Indian staples to plan for that variability explicitly. See our <a href="/products/fresh-vegetables/red-onion/">red onion page</a> for the detail.</p>

<h2>LC lead time is part of your schedule</h2>
<p>Bangladesh trade runs overwhelmingly on letters of credit, and LC opening, amendment and document-checking add real time. Buyers who plan from "order confirmed" rather than "LC operative" consistently find their timelines slipping. Build it in.</p>

